Use short, isolated test paths and inspect descriptor identity on Solaris.

Long service clone paths exceed the socket limit before the test-specific
prefix, and exceed the exact lengths exercised by bug75679.  Use short
per-test paths while retaining all length, socket and output assertions.
Solaris procfs file descriptor entries are not symbolic links; compare the
reopened descriptor device, inode, mode and device number with /dev/null.
This still detects descriptor zero leaking after failed proc_open setup.

Will submit upstream.

